Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/sqlite-replication-ltx.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/sqlite-replication-ltx.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/sqlite-replication-ltx.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:ea860dd7f49bf4fe26c5f8bacf6ef70ff6d100bc41824a9baebe2564f4ae4a00",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ccf9e10b254848e7a274b6d3bddaa37f",
+      "statement": "`celld-ltx` is a from-scratch Rust reimplementation of Litestream v0.5.11 whose block format follows LTX v0.5.2.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/lib.rs#L3-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:572023f3b758b3962bc6ddf1a5e72a502d2c7271eeba457fb88f9657a5043a61:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_09e0a616934e4f39a814c8f45a570cb0",
+      "statement": "The capture API in `db.rs` is kept synchronous and owns the SQLite connection directly because `rusqlite::Connection` is !Sync; `Replica` drives `sync()` and `checkpoint()` from a blocking context.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/db.rs#L8-L18",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:902651f62e851221675a7352a8967032bec1d6d8e07de42f03181b839d6226e3:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1eacd20fcf614f3bbe1b1cab29695257",
+      "statement": "The functional capture path diffs the real WAL against the last LTX position and writes the next L0 LTX file with atomic tmp→rename and a position cache; `verify` is the snapshot-on-continuity-break branch lattice and `checkpoint_if_needed` applies a 3-tier policy with anti-feedback flags.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/db.rs#L20-L47",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:84761fe72c44cd7d25e606a026bbc522c3a1e08eae76b3e109960faf58899b6d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_08c3acb8f656467eb641593136a630c6",
+      "statement": "`CheckpointMode` renders exactly PASSIVE/FULL/RESTART/TRUNCATE into `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(<mode>)`.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/db.rs#L66-L90",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:519c14208d7a67e211205aeb4c183ec7e53ce5aba926c6f3c444e285a549815e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bff3968452f04991814d40541d31d550",
+      "statement": "`Replica` drives two halves of replication: sync copies each new L0 LTX file up to the remote replica advancing the replicated position one TXID at a time, and restore downloads LTX files in TXID order, merges them with the compactor, and reconstructs the SQLite file to a temp file that is fsync'd and atomically renamed into place.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/replica.rs#L4-L16",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3b07712730b28140b79a023830993b590a2447f08345dbca4ea354e43a4c716:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_07d0176019714d22961f9b3c034312f0",
+      "statement": "The restore-plan calculation honors a target TXID and probes the snapshot level first so it stays a faithful port that works when compaction is added; the current scope is L0-only and one-shot.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/replica.rs#L18-L36",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1f84db796afc268115039cc4711f168a8370d87390f0910400f6c4458ead339:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7ccdb6ed4f8644c784f30e1d6e16d409",
+      "statement": "The compactor is a streaming port of the LTX Compactor that merges ordered LTX inputs into one byte-compatible output, keeping one decompressed page per input rather than a database-sized page map.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/compactor.rs#L1-L36",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b040771e73a5a7e77879a26b6dec827b4e01bc87bc981378f76d49de5248d5b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1ca8b42d88d343e289d22e9bc949131e",
+      "statement": "The bundle is a celld-original, self-contained envelope (magic `CLB1`) that concatenates verbatim L0 LTX bytes with a little-endian footer, so un-bundling is pure arithmetic and a drained bundle leaves the bucket in pure-Litestream state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/bundle.rs#L4-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93dabfc5b6779fdfa4da143d89d32bbb2fd5e46af58846f85fa9db52d347f263:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f0b275bb49a24d93a176957652b2ba7c",
+      "statement": "`ReplicaClient` is the storage abstraction every replica backend implements, with `FileReplicaClient` storing on the local filesystem and `ObjectStoreClient` (behind the s3 feature) using the object_store crate.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/lib.rs#L72-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:079345ed3b5ac5d0504fba1d07c80e6a562cbd8a3ba88ce914c2fd1b6717c834:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4e0846c65f464ac380477f48440c59a4",
+      "statement": "The unstable `internal` module with no compatibility guarantee re-exports db, lz4_block, replica, and object_store internals for external verification tools.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/lib.rs#L30-L41",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66cbccaf91b8a45115f3a0fdcf4cef55c0d58b3e8694abff8f02288cb847f433:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0a9da9c4d584426f9586b0ed47716651",
+      "statement": "celld's `crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs` builds its own object-store clients rather than going through `bucket::Bucket` and carries the fleet's key prefix itself, so two fleets sharing one bucket do not replicate over each other.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L11-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5c59ca3acd77a1ebfd460cdb32818f760bffcee3551b9e4489c935e262f0425:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:37:50.122Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/v8-isolate-hosts.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/v8-isolate-hosts.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/v8-isolate-hosts.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:5f596b2bea19cd329222cc6146bc957a060caeb9ecca8dc4f18d95d42ae684cd",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a46fa81fc472436ba02459f0c102078d",
+      "statement": "celld embeds `rusty_v8` directly with one isolate per cell, running actual Durable Objects where `env.NS.get(id).fetch()` instantiates the exported DO class once per id with a `state` whose `storage` is backed by the cell's SQLite.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L8-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3d6723fd7461ff73e7bdc96a3de3ba2066f8cf9005123a51731700b09dd97a2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8cfeb803f9ab46ed881e103080747576",
+      "statement": "DO storage is async in JS but synchronous underneath, because the ops are sync Rust wrapped in `async` by the JS harness.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L13-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c748d25ec3c928c85221bfcfd2e28f797ea9bb38edc90141830238c96aa03d22:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9296bbf7c760460dbf804862f400f1dc",
+      "statement": "celld keeps a per-process compiled-bytecode cache of the ~23k lines of prelude and harness; the first isolate compiles eagerly and publishes the cache and every later isolate consumes it, so a fresh cell wake pays only execution, not compilation.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/bootstrap.rs#L3-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28af0d1860eeb23fcb5f4cb7e070bec293c228c4b4df4f5d01f7a2722459f982:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_51edd66a580c4ac8a01fe543675792d2",
+      "statement": "The bindings (`env`, routing table, compatibility flags) differ per worker and are built every time on top of the cached prelude and harness.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/bootstrap.rs#L6-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fe317c0d745d4365f6081b1be11abfe8f408d3e7281c7648c6814ed5e9543bb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b88bbb2377e44c1bb6580cb789c09250",
+      "statement": "ES module resolution treats a specifier as either a builtin whose source the module holds or an import of another worker resolved through the loader; most builtins are lazy and compile only when something reads their global.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/modules.rs#L3-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9bed57565fc003f502c43b47e330681c01d9e4d9f7b13225bfbcd17dc1b3c1d1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_821aa781eb0a43ba9ceda58e5460a1a3",
+      "statement": "The module registry is an isolate slot, not a thread-local, so `Global<Module>` handles into one isolate's heap never leak across isolates.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/modules.rs#L38-L54",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8f034b45adf09dcc15654972bfe5d5baac48b10ad926fd49b28305073258e04:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d45e545f0b77459694bf91fd08e72f24",
+      "statement": "`storage_ops.rs` is the V8 surface over `crate::storage` for key-value, SQL, and the shared value encoding; it converts V8 values to Rust, calls into storage, and converts the answer back, deciding nothing.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/storage_ops.rs#L3-L9",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b47d75d184ab5f2a9199eb8469fd0162a376b9928728d8f4a054795ddfcc9a5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c9ffe9f027834358978371fbe4660b3d",
+      "statement": "When an isolate hits `env.NS.get(id)` for a cell this node does not own, the op hands the request to the tokio runtime, which resolves the owner and HTTP-proxies the fetch, replying on an async oneshot so the JS thread is never blocked.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L83-L90",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06ee7064393508791e0fecb480d1a99b26ac9cd035e35c2c1b258bb66b675e65:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d8a4b717b18048108544eccdfca45e48",
+      "statement": "`RuntimeManager` in `crates/celld/runtime.rs` is the V8 cell-host arm that owns handles and filesystem paths but never lifecycle policy; `StartRuntime`, `Publish`, and `StopRuntime` decide when a cell handle moves from starting to externally dispatchable to closed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/runtime.rs#L7-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77b63e2f9b042e414f073fd784ad551ee064a7f5f6c3e972ea2ecce576a948c1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ecc8d07998da4de5929e894be6ba78c1",
+      "statement": "celld implements a Partial subset of Cloudflare Workers, Durable Objects, Cron Triggers, Worker Loader, KV, Queues, D1, Workflows, and R2, with Static assets, Encoding, and WebAssembly as Yes and Workers AI, Facets, Cache, HTMLRewriter, TCP sockets, EventSource, MessageChannel, and BroadcastChannel as No.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/cloudflare-compat.md#L15-L183",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76052bc19d6fbbc3d283560f1980db66a2f07930aa6bb0115ff2c2c1af2de513:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_aed3bc0ad572420dafdde1be818cf385",
+      "statement": "celld honors the compatibility switches `delete_all_deletes_alarm`, `js_rpc`, `fetcher_no_get_put_delete`, `sqlite_vec`, `websocket_standard_binary_type`, and the static-assets navigation flags, computed from the worker's compatibility_date/flags metadata by `worker_compat`; other flags are accepted without effect.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L483-L522",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c367993fb8c0653f13ab6dfe873544512478f6fd231c142e6b5d6e3f6e379d8:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/cloudflare-compat.md#L305-L317",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:968925eddd7341978787d8817371451342f7dda5892952239a84264112549baa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a7941f91bc0c4eeebe751bc403a1813b",
+      "statement": "`celld deploy` accepts `wrangler.jsonc` or `wrangler.json` with a defined subset of top-level keys, and each other top-level key (including `routes`) stops the deployment.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/cloudflare-compat.md#L319-L333",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19a37e6c8e285d75a7a4e521de84e9a1d57a50bb65e96ffbed45cacc7de085f0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b748945353524b5fafcf38f6ffa5d20d",
+      "statement": "The raw V8 adapter and its child modules remain outside the Actor execution domain; the Actor-reachable wake and WebSocket state is injected through HostServices, so the deterministic simulator can drive the lifecycle core while V8 stays out of simulation because V8 is not deterministic.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L3-L6",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6af73672c48a37650765efd11f28dedd2d95c7495e07274da17d8f408600a46a:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L94-L95",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c72d23949ee79855726e8cbb46b2e861ee3c0613687881e8f718bfb7417e6de4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:37:50.122Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/operations/configuration.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/operations/configuration.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/operations/configuration.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:c738cd2f8c0acd1ae45747f12e97b2b190ce0745b98acf659bb02ad602d3bf3e",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_31ccd614e1004295bb48ceb7b62d0667",
+      "statement": "Two conditional-write dialects share one object-store client surface: S3 and Azure speak the etag dialect with If-Match/If-None-Match, while GCS speaks the Cloud Storage XML API generation dialect with x-goog-if-generation-match; the distinction is the dialect, not the endpoint.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L7-L18",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b01da9526b4227977abf4647655d591fd57987ed560ba8ef2cf623ec12d5653:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4482d41a71524abebf2e3b2348780266",
+      "statement": "`put_cas` answers `Ok(None)` only for a clean 412/409 rejection and every other failure is ambiguous because the write may have committed; a response carrying no CAS token is an error, not an empty token.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L20-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87a60adc0e4f479dd4365a62475a2c87612ec70a014849fa56ebd9b221395daa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_478b06b174934bc9accd97bcc255f9b7",
+      "statement": "The CLI and environment values feed the same `Settings`, and `Action` distinguishes running a node from the operator subcommands deploy, dev, cell, d1, kv, queue, connect, credentials, token, disconnect, and diagnose.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L9-L54",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5e7538fab550cedf536014470222f24dc5f1be2e984198c3bac65be0c5814d7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8869465a5f9248a685f674f865beb820",
+      "statement": "celld reserves the probe/, cells/, nodes/, node-cells/, fleet/, deploy/, deploy-blobs/, wake/, and telemetry/ prefixes and deletes objects under some of them, so an application must not write under them.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L78-L81",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20f67018001ec0d74645b241a61691ebcf6b71f9236f3b1d3987094e055609e9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c596d656ecef4254b4192e3949e6338a",
+      "statement": "A bucket PREFIX puts every object under it so several fleets can share one bucket, and the cli modality accepts s3://, gs://, or az:// with the respective credential chain.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L288-L296",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:515bdff11eb476f274f6f2c52ab0ce6a687d82d3c74492acf0c470a5d7eea266:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bd91082a22354e319ffdf13762a3dd4f",
+      "statement": "An R2 binding uses the fleet bucket under the additional prefix `r2/<bucket_name>/`.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/cloudflare-compat.md#L145-L149",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d86d536aa3c69206023ab1be1c51d2ae555c98cb2fb20fe21722270ca9f1d3e5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fa83f26f67b54a618fd4933b5fd7fee0",
+      "statement": "`CELLD_DURABILITY` defaults to `fleet` and must be exactly `bucket` or `fleet`; `fleet` acks when every follower holds the write on disk or when the bucket upload wins country pushes, and a fleet of one node does not get it while `bucket` always waits for the bucket.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L3721-L3726",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa07a549d74e8eb564b7bae7d9bccf1092ba2d501cb44d62c1d0e4a7035ff858:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L372-L378",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bf3ec8b24db71b961d7d2b6fd91678218e21a448bba5e1c4342d28160be9daf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_efcf627ba2bd4c4dbb2dca10e87069af",
+      "statement": "`CELLD_TTL_MS` sets the node lease lifetime and defaults to 10000 ms.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/machine.rs#L53-L55",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32804d7b58095664daccbe3c196efb6179785f005f9e34c9ea77ef369e7669ba:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2d551c37f1074b3186dbcb995fd63cef",
+      "statement": "`CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS` is an optional hard resident-cell cap enforced at admission with no value meaning unbounded (usize::MAX).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L3166-L3171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e82ad0155a9c18b7bc1345740ee24370344bce01bdc70b3f4985fafae525c187:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8a9b1001307a4347adaabae390275ddd",
+      "statement": "Every typed production environment variable is validated before the runtime starts; a boolean accepts only 0/1, a positive variable must be greater than zero, so a typo cannot silently change the configuration of a running node.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L16-L100",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6332b269fec1f48ea97c910cfabf4d650c9f71514a091a15d1b1ad97eea9081a:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L3-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:659b779fbef4e2889c1649b6c55457564394919e2f392d99b534641d5bef3807:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a75b66b9aa4740ca953a38ebe2c1454f",
+      "statement": "The CLI is strict: a non-loopback --listen or CELLD_ADDR requires an explicit --internal-listen/CELLD_INTERNAL_ADDR, and --advertise/CELLD_ADVERTISE requires an explicit internal listener, because celld does not reuse the public Worker listener for peer traffic.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L236-L246",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0294eba5fed02e36288c786242ff7d210293bfe6e50542ef765ff009369ff0c9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
